title ALES65 — Lotus's keyed gate: the door opened by another signal
prompt baton prin recur — continue the ALES ladder Lindy-first crux-first, sending each finished increment as its own signed round
think ALES63 named three tools its keyed detector unlocks: de-esser, ducker, keyed gate. ALES64 built the de-esser. Crux-first, the keyed gate is the third named tool and the exact mirror of the sidechain compressor — where the compressor ducks the target when the key gets loud (above threshold), the gate opens the target when the key is loud and closes it when quiet (below threshold).
think Uses (a click track gating a pad to the beat, a tom gated by its own close mic to kill kit bleed, a synth chopped by a drum loop) — all one keyed primitive.
think Design: lotus/gate_key.rye mirrors ALES63's sidechain pair with the read-only key beside the mutable target, carrying env + hold_left. Advance hold_env.env_step_hold on the key; at/above threshold the target passes, below it the target is attenuated by ALES51's floor.
think The load-bearing correctness care the compressor never faced: the gate acts BELOW the threshold, so a keyed detector can read exact silence from the KEY (e == 0) while the TARGET is loud — the fully-closed gate. ALES57 divides through the envelope (gat/e), undefined at e == 0. But that gain is algebraically den/num (the envelope cancels: (e·den/num)/e = den/num), so the e == 0 branch applies den/num directly — no divide by zero. For a self-key a zero key envelope means a zero target sample, so it writes zero over zero, byte-for-byte with ALES57. This preserves the grounding law AND handles the silent-key/loud-target case correctly.
obs GREEN on the first build across eight clauses: silence; self-key == ALES57 byte-for-byte (grounding); a loud key opens the gate (quiet target passes whole where the in-line gate silences it, proven against ALES57); a silent key closes the gate (loud target attenuated where the in-line gate passes it — the e == 0 branch, proven both ways against ALES57); unit ratio identity even under a silent key; sign held / magnitude never expands; state carries (env + hold_left) so a mid-hold split equals the whole; and BadThreshold/BadRatio/BadCoeff/BadHold/BadRange/BadKey each refuse by name.
obs This completes the keyed wing — all three tools ALES63 named now stand as compositions of proven parts. The ducker is the sidechain read with an external voice key (already proven behaviorally in ALES63); the keyed gate is its mirror.
loom witness=ales_gate_key_witness green=yes clauses=8 reproofs=2 tame_bans=clean
file lotus/gate_key.rye ALES65 module — gate_key_follow / gate_key_follow_carry, the e==0 silent-key branch, GREEN selftest
file tools/ales_gate_key_witness.rish witness — builds and runs the selftest, re-proves ALES57 and ALES56 beside it, GREEN
